3:`native_explosion_entities(dimension, center, entities)` (server) runs after `native_explosion_detonate`, before an explosion at `center` hurts and pushes anything: `entities` holds the ids of the entities in its reach (`ServerExplosion.hurtEntities`), players aside, which `native_living_incoming_damage` hears. Take out the ids to spare: they are neither hurt nor pushed, as NeoForge's `ExplosionEvent.Detonate` does with its entity list. Bundles need "hooks": 644.
5:`native_chat_suggestion_applied(original, start, end, suggestion, input)` reports a suggestion accepted in the open chat by Tab or a mouse click, after the text and caret have changed. `original` is the suggestion list's input before any completion; `start` and `end` are the replaced range in that string, in Java UTF-16 units (end exclusive). They keep referring to `original` when Tab cycles through the list. `suggestion` is the selected replacement text, and `input` is the actual resulting field value, including any length-limit truncation. This is a read-only notification: previews, list navigation, server replies, ordinary typing and command-block editors do not fire it. Trait mods implement `Hooks::chat_suggestion_applied`; mixin bundles use `chat_suggestion_applied`, hook version 1. Bundles need "hooks": 566 (assigned at merge).
7:API 362 adds `native_compute_fov_modifier(player, base, modifier)` on the client each tick for the local player's FOV scale, after vanilla effects and before zoom and camera easing. `player` contains the calculation inputs and `base` is the original scale. Non-finite modifiers or values outside 0.01..=10 fall back to `base`. It does not affect a spectator camera on a mob. Bundles need "hooks": 362.
9:The client hook `native_client_packet(packet)` hears each play packet the server sends, decoded (`ClientboundPlayPacket`, `horizon_protocol`'s `play::Clientbound`), just before the game handles it, custom payloads included and in the order they came. It only reads: the game handles the packet as it would without the mod. Packets the network thread handles itself (keep-alives, bundle delimiters, resource packs, cookies, server links, transfers, disconnects, the configuration switch, `minecraft:brand`, far terrain tiles) and the configuration phase are not heard. Bundles need "hooks": 408.
11:`native_registry_name(registry, id)` (`host.registry_name`) is the name of a protocol id in a registry: `minecraft:item`, `minecraft:data_component_type`, `minecraft:entity_type`, `minecraft:sound_event`, `minecraft:particle_type` and the like. It names what `native_client_packet`'s packets carry as numbers (a `Stack`'s item and components, `AddEntity`'s type, `Sound`, `LevelParticles`). On a client the ids are those of the server it is connected to, so a registry the server synced (enchantments, painting variants) and a mod's own data components, when the server carries them, name too; on a server they are the ids it sends. It answers `None` for an unknown registry, an id out of range or negative, and while no server is connected. Bundles need `"hooks": 637`.
